                    <name>15</name>
                    <description>GPA.15 wake-up function Enabled</description>
                    <value>#1111</value>
                 </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DBEN</name>
              <description>GPA Input Signal De-bounce Enable Bit\nThe DBEN bit is used to enable the de-bounce function for each corresponding I/O. If the input signal pulse width cannot be sampled by continuous two de-bounce sample cycle, the input signal transition is seen as the signal bounce and will not trigger the wake-up.The de-bounce clock source is the 10 kHz internal low speed RC oscillator (LIRC).\nThe de-bounce function is valid only for edgetriggered.</description>
              <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <enumeratedValues>
